nd pop culture in general has painted a  rather large  target on the back of a group of voters  than being trump voters which forces  them into the shadows  so when you talk about shy voters we're  only  under counting trump voters people are  only  lying that they're voting for joe they  aren't lying  voting for trump because why would you  vote why would you lie about something  that would get you  abused that would that's like going to  the doctor and telling him  that you're smoking more no no no no  when you're gonna lie to your doctor  you're gonna tell him that you've lost  weight  and that you're you you've cut your  smoking in half  so there's a really simple experiment  for the media to do go to a trump event  in a biden shirt then go to a binding  event in a trump shirt and  compare and contrast and see how people  treat you lastly to the derogatory story  in the atlantic i need to comment on  that  you need to have an anonymous story like  that  when there's an economic recovery a jobs  recovery and hopefully a strong path to  corral coven which i think is happening  so you need stuff like this  but the funniest thing about the  atlantic story and this upcoming michael  cohen book they're like a farmer's  almanac that tells you the weather that  already happened  right so wait a second you're telling me  that  trump says offensive things in public  oh my god what do we do we've only known  that for four years  maybe even longer than that and lastly  for the journalists out there let's come  up with a  real definition of what confirmation  means because confirmation  of an unproven allegation from a source  isn't a confirmation of fact it's a  confirmation of an unproven allegation  all right let me ask you about this  emily there's this other factor in north  carolina  where the polls are tightening perhaps  but i think republicans are a little bit  more stressed out about the fact  that when it comes to early voting and  absentee ballot requests  the de